From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:02:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09359/11362] Compacted carried state for the induction tool
 loop (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6540)

The tool loop drops reasoning_content between turns and caps per-turn thinking,
but the message list still grows without bound. Every assistant turn and every
full tool-result JSON stays in the conversation for the rest of the loop.

This adds a bounded carried state behind CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_TOOL_COMPACT. Unset,
or any value other than "1", is byte-identical to today.

Why it matters. Two constraints on the scored run are both context-length
effects. Decode falls from 42.4 tok/s at 10k tokens to 29.0 tok/s at 80k on the
scored card, measured. KV per stream caps how many inductions run at once, and
the agent framework starts one thread PER GAME with no pool, so surplus requests
queue against a fixed 2400s per-call timeout while generating nothing. Shorter
per-turn context helps decode rate, stream count, and queue wait together.

The carried state is built mechanically from the candidate list and tool
results. There is no summarizer call: adding inference inside the loop would
defeat the purpose and could invent facts. Compaction is threshold-triggered
rather than per-turn, so prefix caching survives between events, and the unit is
a complete round, so no tool message is orphaned from its call.

Dropped detail is re-fetchable. Every tool is a deterministic pure function of
a fixed window, so the model can recover evidence at one prefill-priced call.
The only irrecoverable loss is assistant prose and superseded candidate source,
whose scores and hashes are kept.

The byte-identity pin is proven by mutation, not by assertion. Making
compaction_enabled() return True unconditionally fails it by name:
"compaction machinery consulted with env unset". 51 tests pass, and git status
before and after the run is identical, so the suite rewrites no tracked files.

No default is flipped. The env var appears nowhere outside its own module and
tests. An adversarial review of this change is in flight; findings will land as
follow-ups rather than by amending this commit.

